          },
          {
            "dimension": "register-lanes",
            "requirement": "MODE axis (the second register axis): wherever the player and an NPC are present and something is said, carry it in dialog blocks (their words/refusals/scheming do the character work), NOT a narrated summary of the exchange. Lean HARDEST at the hot beats (capstone/sex/confrontation) — narrating those as summary is the single worst drift. Multi-party = each present NPC gets a short voiced beat (no monologues). Narration is right ONLY when no one's there to speak (solo, unseen voyeur/peek, capstone interior monologue); a present NPC always gets at least one terse line.",
            "citation": "rts-flat-prose.md:68-74 (Rule 4); lanes.md:331-339 ('Mode, not just density'); beat-authoring.md:117-126,238-248; SKILL.md:86-90",
            "verbatim": "where a beat is an exchange, carry it in `dialog` blocks (their words, interruptions, refusals), never a narrated summary ... Lean hardest at the hot beats ... narrating the encounter as summary is the worst drift — play them."
          },
          {
            "dimension": "register-lanes",
            "requirement": "The 8 mechanical Lane 1/2/3 prose rules: (1) second-person 'you'; (2) stage-direction cap 2 sentences/beat; (3) ZERO environmental sensory detail (no smell/window-light/kettle — the HUD carries world state); (4) dialogue does character work, not narration; (5) no inferential/backstory prose (Tier-3 only); (6) direct/crude diction at sexual register (real anatomical terms, at the NPC's per-tier vocab ceiling, default-to-maximum-explicit); (7) one beat = one click; (8) image-first composition.",
            "citation": "rts-flat-prose.md:44-110 (§2 Rules 1-8)",
            "verbatim": "No smell, no window light, no kettle clicks, no dust motes, no coffee aroma. The HUD carries world state ... prose that paints the kitchen is doing world-grounding the HUD already does, and pays for it on every re-read."
          },
          {
            "dimension": "register-lanes",
            "requirement": "Choice labels are tighter than prose: terse action verb = the action, flavor lives in the opened scene not the label; strip self-justifying subtext; put the crude word IN the label at the NPC's ceiling ('Suck his cock', not 'Go down on him'); emoji on hub/menu buttons, bare on in-loop cascade beats.",
            "citation": "rts-flat-prose.md:114-123 (§3); lanes.md:113-119 (Lane 1 labels); beat-authoring.md:282-283",
            "verbatim": "A choice label is a terse action verb, and the flavor lives in the scene the click opens, NOT in the label ... At explicit tiers put the crude word IN the label at the NPC's ceiling"
          },
          {
            "dimension": "beat-authoring-process",
            "requirement": "Step 7 authors EXACTLY ONE beat per turn: propose the next beat (ideate -> ask-or-inform) -> mark active -> amend structure WHOLE if needed -> author canvases across the right lanes (translate the blueprint, don't re-decide) -> author/update quest card -> VALIDATE (merge --validate + package_from_toml + doctrine self-audit) -> fix red before marking done -> mark validated + persist ledger. One beat, validate it, then STOP. This is run-mode's ideate->decide->write->verify-green in engineering form.",
            "citation": "beat-authoring.md:1-8 (header), 85-140 (the beat loop), 142-288 (validation); run-mode.md:58-65 (per-increment rhythm)",
            "verbatim": "Author exactly one per turn, validate it, then stop. This is `run-mode.md`'s \"ideate -> decide -> write -> **verify green**\" rhythm in engineering form"
          },
          {
            "dimension": "beat-authoring-process",
            "requirement": "Every increment BUILDS GREEN before the next leans on it. A red build is a STOP, not a footnote. Validation order: (1) merge_toml_phases --validate (syntax only); (2) package_from_toml --dev (the REAL validation: schema, broken refs, flag chains, builds index.html — never skip); (3) the doctrine self-audit checklist (~25 line items). Any FAIL -> fix, re-run, then mark validated.",
            "citation": "beat-authoring.md:142-288; run-mode.md:115 (Law-3 build-green)",
            "verbatim": "Every increment **BUILDS GREEN** before the next (Step 7). A red build is a stop, not a footnote."
          },
          {
            "dimension": "beat-authoring-process",
            "requirement": "Each beat must NAME the WANT it serves (the desire ladder) and be framed as pursuing that want — a beat whose only justification is 'raises a meter' is grind: cut or reframe.",
