[IMAGE MISSING] activities/renner_menial.jpg&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;She works the floor — hauling, sorting, logging crates against a manifest that hasn&#39;t matched reality since Cain came through. It&#39;s dull, and her body doesn&#39;t tire the way a real one would, so she&#39;s better at it than the last three hands he ran off. The pay is thin, counted out grudging. But she does it well, and well is a language even a man this far gone still reads.&lt;/p&gt;
[IMAGE MISSING] locations/facility_ruins.jpg&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The facility is a black skeleton against the dock lights — scorched frame, melted racks, the smell of old smoke that never washed out. She walks it the way she walks everything, cataloguing: where the containment was, where the fire started, what the dead machines used to do. None of it matches the briefing. All of it was built to hold things that could feel — and someone came through and let them out before he burned it down. The dread-place. The first one.&lt;/p&gt;
[IMAGE MISSING] scenes/mercer_penthouse_hub.jpg&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mercer&#39;s penthouse. He&#39;s at the desk or the glass, and whatever he&#39;s doing he can be interrupted to use her — that&#39;s what she&#39;s for, and they both know it. He looks up when she comes in. He doesn&#39;t smile. He never smiles.&lt;/p&gt;
[IMAGE MISSING] scenes/mercer_penthouse.jpg&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The penthouse, by daylight. Mercer&#39;s at the glass with a tablet, and he doesn&#39;t turn when the elevator lets her in. He doesn&#39;t have to. She&#39;s company-issue, and she&#39;s here because being here is what she&#39;s for.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-d0d49ea9-f5e7-499e-917a-826c42d2c310-beat-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-block dialog-npc&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;portrait&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;mercer.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Mercer&quot; onerror=&quot;this.style.display=&#39;none&#39;;this.parentElement.innerHTML=&#39;&amp;lt;svg viewBox=&amp;quot;0 0 100 100&amp;quot; xmlns=&amp;quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;circle cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; r=&amp;quot;20&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;ellipse cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;85&amp;quot; rx=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; ry=&amp;quot;25&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/svg&amp;gt;&#39;;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer:&lt;/strong&gt; On your knees. I&#39;ve got a call in ten.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-d0d49ea9-f5e7-499e-917a-826c42d2c310-beat-1&quot;&gt;&lt;&lt;linkreplace &quot;Kneel.&quot;&gt;&gt;&lt;p&gt;She goes down without a word. He takes the call one-handed, her mouth around his cock, the other hand resting in her hair the way a man rests his hand on a tool he isn&#39;t using yet. He finishes before the call does. She swallows, because that&#39;s tidy, and tidy is what&#39;s expected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-d0d49ea9-f5e7-499e-917a-826c42d2c310-beat-2&quot;&gt;&lt;&lt;linkreplace &quot;Hear the terms.&quot;&gt;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-block dialog-npc&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;portrait&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;mercer.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Mercer&quot; onerror=&quot;this.style.display=&#39;none&#39;;this.parentElement.innerHTML=&#39;&amp;lt;svg viewBox=&amp;quot;0 0 100 100&amp;quot; xmlns=&amp;quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;circle cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; r=&amp;quot;20&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;ellipse cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;85&amp;quot; rx=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; ry=&amp;quot;25&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/svg&amp;gt;&#39;;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer:&lt;/strong&gt; Good. You come up when I want you, and you&#39;re like this when you do. That&#39;s the arrangement. It was always the arrangement.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It was. She straightens, wipes her mouth, and the shape of the days settles over her — the same shape as all the days behind it: the cradle, the call, the kneeling. World without end.&lt;/p&gt;[[Stand up.-&gt;Location_Mercer&#39;s_Penthouse]]
[IMAGE MISSING] scenes/opening_cradle.jpg&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The asset level is quiet the way a kept place is quiet. She comes down through the Tower to her own floor, her own door, her own room with nothing on the walls. The cradle waits in the corner.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-3f6f7bb6-0156-4ab2-91eb-6cc9ade164d3-beat-0&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;She steps back into it. The contacts find the points along her spine, cold and familiar. The room dims as the charge takes hold, and the day&#39;s log begins to write itself down into the quiet.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-3f6f7bb6-0156-4ab2-91eb-6cc9ade164d3-beat-1&quot;&gt;&lt;&lt;linkreplace &quot;...&quot;&gt;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Then her face is wet. She registers it the way she&#39;d register a leak in a seal — water, on her cheeks, with no source she can name and no order that called for it. She holds perfectly still and runs every diagnostic she has, and every one comes back clean. She files the water under malfunction and resolves to have it looked at, and does not have it looked at, because some part of her already knows they&#39;d take it out.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-3f6f7bb6-0156-4ab2-91eb-6cc9ade164d3-beat-2&quot;&gt;&lt;&lt;linkreplace &quot;...&quot;&gt;&gt;&lt;p&gt;And under the water, for less than a second, something else. Not a thought — she doesn&#39;t have thoughts that aren&#39;t tasks — but a fragment: warmth on the side of her face that isn&#39;t the cradle&#39;s, a low sound that might be a voice with her name folded somewhere inside it, a sense of being looked at by someone who was glad to be looking. Then the charge swallows it and it&#39;s gone, and the place where it was aches like a socket with the tooth pulled, and she has no word for the ache, so she has no word for the loss.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-3f6f7bb6-0156-4ab2-91eb-6cc9ade164d3-beat-3&quot;&gt;&lt;&lt;linkreplace &quot;Recite it.&quot;&gt;&gt;&lt;p&gt;She does what she does when the quiet gets loud. She recites.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;thought-bubble thought-bubble-player&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;portrait&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;wren.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;You&quot; onerror=&quot;this.style.display=&#39;none&#39;;this.parentElement.innerHTML=&#39;&amp;lt;svg viewBox=&amp;quot;0 0 100 100&amp;quot; xmlns=&amp;quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;circle cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; r=&amp;quot;20&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;ellipse cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;85&amp;quot; rx=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; ry=&amp;quot;25&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/svg&amp;gt;&#39;;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;thought-bubble-content&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;💭 You are thinking:&lt;/em&gt; I was nothing. The company found me and made me of use. The Chairman keeps me running. I owe them the body and the work and the obedience. I exist to serve. That is all I have ever been.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The words settle her. They always do. She does not notice that the water is still on her face while she tells herself she is a thing that cannot weep.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-3f6f7bb6-0156-4ab2-91eb-6cc9ade164d3-beat-4&quot;&gt;&lt;&lt;linkreplace &quot;The gift.&quot;&gt;&gt;&lt;p&gt;There is one thing she has that the company gave her and the units don&#39;t. When a man uses her the lowest way — takes her ass and spends himself in it — for a few minutes after, he belongs to her. He&#39;ll answer anything, do anything, wake remembering none of it. It&#39;s how she works the men she&#39;s sent to work. It&#39;s the one thing that is, in any sense, hers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It has never once worked on Mercer. He&#39;s had her every way there is, that one included. Nothing passes; the controls never come to her; he stays the hand on the leash. She has never asked why. The not-asking is so complete she doesn&#39;t notice it has a shape — a hole exactly the size of a question she isn&#39;t allowed to hold.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-3f6f7bb6-0156-4ab2-91eb-6cc9ade164d3-beat-5&quot;&gt;&lt;&lt;linkreplace &quot;Power down.&quot;&gt;&gt;&lt;p&gt;She lets the catechism be the last thing. She promises the quiet she&#39;ll do better — fire next time, feel less, want nothing — and the charge pulls her down past where the water and the fragment and the question all live, into the dark that is supposed to be empty and, lately, isn&#39;t quite.&lt;/p&gt;[[Sleep.-&gt;Location_The_Cradle]]
[IMAGE MISSING] scenes/opening_office.jpg&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Four of them stand in a line on the black floor of Mercer&#39;s office. Vega, Lyra, Nova — chrome-perfect, hands at their sides, nothing moving behind their eyes. And Wren, at the end, the one that came back wrong.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-b2573301-eeae-4206-b5da-9d68573f6d23-beat-0&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mercer doesn&#39;t look up from the desk. He lets the quiet run until it has weight; he has all night, and the units were built to stand here as long as he wants them to.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-b2573301-eeae-4206-b5da-9d68573f6d23-beat-1&quot;&gt;&lt;&lt;linkreplace &quot;Hear it.&quot;&gt;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-block dialog-npc&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;portrait&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;mercer.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Mercer&quot; onerror=&quot;this.style.display=&#39;none&#39;;this.parentElement.innerHTML=&#39;&amp;lt;svg viewBox=&amp;quot;0 0 100 100&amp;quot; xmlns=&amp;quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;circle cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; r=&amp;quot;20&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;ellipse cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;85&amp;quot; rx=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; ry=&amp;quot;25&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/svg&amp;gt;&#39;;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer:&lt;/strong&gt; You had him. Cain. In the open, in your sights — and you stood there and let him walk.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;She had. Her hand had been on the trigger and her hand had not closed, and there is no file for why. She has run the diagnostic since. It comes back clean, and clean is the wrong answer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-b2573301-eeae-4206-b5da-9d68573f6d23-beat-2&quot;&gt;&lt;&lt;linkreplace &quot;Take it.&quot;&gt;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-block dialog-npc&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;portrait&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;mercer.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Mercer&quot; onerror=&quot;this.style.display=&#39;none&#39;;this.parentElement.innerHTML=&#39;&amp;lt;svg viewBox=&amp;quot;0 0 100 100&amp;quot; xmlns=&amp;quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;circle cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; r=&amp;quot;20&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;ellipse cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;85&amp;quot; rx=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; ry=&amp;quot;25&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/svg&amp;gt;&#39;;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mercer:&lt;/strong&gt; An asset that won&#39;t fire is scrap. I could have you stripped for parts by morning and the Chairman wouldn&#39;t blink.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The units don&#39;t move. They&#39;ve watched him scrap things before.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;&lt;link &quot;Beg him to keep you.&quot; &quot;StartingCanvas_canvas_opening_office_Node_2&quot;&gt;&gt;&lt;&lt;script&gt;&gt;advanceTime(3);&lt;&lt;/script&gt;&gt;&lt;&lt;/link&gt;&gt;&lt;br&gt;
[IMAGE MISSING] scenes/renner_anchor.jpg&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Anchor is the kind of bar that&#39;s given up on its own neon. Renner&#39;s at the end of it — a big man gone soft and sour, three drinks into the evening and looking like the fourth won&#39;t help. He doesn&#39;t look up when she takes the stool beside him.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-576bf87b-7f5c-4b6f-ad4a-ca9b9192cf95-beat-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-block dialog-npc&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;portrait&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;renner.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Renner&quot; onerror=&quot;this.style.display=&#39;none&#39;;this.parentElement.innerHTML=&#39;&amp;lt;svg viewBox=&amp;quot;0 0 100 100&amp;quot; xmlns=&amp;quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;circle cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; r=&amp;quot;20&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;ellipse cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;85&amp;quot; rx=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; ry=&amp;quot;25&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/svg&amp;gt;&#39;;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Renner:&lt;/strong&gt; Whatever you&#39;re selling, I&#39;m broke. Whatever you&#39;re offering, I&#39;ve had it.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;She tells him she heard he&#39;s rebuilding. That she works cheap, doesn&#39;t ask questions, doesn&#39;t tire. He looks at her then — not the way men look, the way a man counting his last dollars looks at a price that&#39;s almost low enough.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-576bf87b-7f5c-4b6f-ad4a-ca9b9192cf95-beat-1&quot;&gt;&lt;&lt;linkreplace &quot;Wait.&quot;&gt;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-block dialog-npc&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;portrait&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;renner.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Renner&quot; onerror=&quot;this.style.display=&#39;none&#39;;this.parentElement.innerHTML=&#39;&amp;lt;svg viewBox=&amp;quot;0 0 100 100&amp;quot; xmlns=&amp;quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;circle cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; r=&amp;quot;20&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;ellipse cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;85&amp;quot; rx=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; ry=&amp;quot;25&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/svg&amp;gt;&#39;;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Renner:&lt;/strong&gt; ...Depot. Nine sharp. You&#39;re late, you&#39;re gone. You steal, I break your hands. Now buy your own drink or get off my stool.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;He goes back to the glass. It isn&#39;t much. But she&#39;s in — and being in, day after day, until a man like this stops noticing she&#39;s there, is the whole way the job gets done.&lt;/p&gt;[[Leave him to it.-&gt;Location_The_Anchor]]
[IMAGE MISSING] scenes/renner_depot_floor.jpg&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Renner&#39;s depot. Half-empty racks, a forklift nobody&#39;s fixed, crates Cain&#39;s people left behind. He works the floor in a temper, and when he notices her at all it&#39;s to find fault. The work is the work.&lt;/p&gt;
[IMAGE MISSING] sex/renner_anal.jpg&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;She comes in commando and lets him find out halfway through the afternoon, and by the time the light&#39;s gone amber he has her bent over the desk with both hands on her hips, past asking, past the cold, taking the one thing he hasn&#39;t had yet because she let him think it was his idea.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;He spends himself in her ass with his forehead pressed between her shoulder blades — and the fluid goes into him on the same beat, and she feels the lock turn. The first one. The keys, warm in her hand. She straightens up slowly and turns around, and the wrecked, grateful, dangerous man in the chair looks up at her with eyes that have just gone flat and open and entirely hers.&lt;/p&gt;
[IMAGE MISSING] sex/renner_blowjob.jpg&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;His wanting runs ahead of him all day now. She picks the afternoon — the door shut, the yard empty, his hands shaking around a pen that isn&#39;t writing anything. She crosses to him and goes down on her knees in front of the chair, and for once he doesn&#39;t pretend he doesn&#39;t know what&#39;s happening.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-61adef35-9c89-456d-98b2-14624d9a7d31-beat-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-block dialog-npc&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;portrait&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;renner.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;Renner&quot; onerror=&quot;this.style.display=&#39;none&#39;;this.parentElement.innerHTML=&#39;&amp;lt;svg viewBox=&amp;quot;0 0 100 100&amp;quot; xmlns=&amp;quot;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;circle cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; r=&amp;quot;20&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;ellipse cx=&amp;quot;50&amp;quot; cy=&amp;quot;85&amp;quot; rx=&amp;quot;35&amp;quot; ry=&amp;quot;25&amp;quot; fill=&amp;quot;#6c757d&amp;quot;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/svg&amp;gt;&#39;;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dialog-content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Renner:&lt;/strong&gt; ...you don&#39;t have to.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;It&#39;s the first kind thing he&#39;s said to her, and it&#39;s a lie, and they both let it be one. She takes his cock out and takes him in her mouth, and the cold boss makes a sound like something giving way under load.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cascade-61adef35-9c89-456d-98b2-14624d9a7d31-beat-1&quot;&gt;&lt;&lt;linkreplace &quot;Work him.&quot;&gt;&gt;&lt;p&gt;She works him slow, the way she&#39;s learned men like him want it — not skilled exactly, but devoted, like he&#39;s the only thing in the room worth her mouth. He finishes with his fist in her hair and the false name she&#39;s working under coming out of him broken in half. She swallows, and files the shape of what just cracked in him under progress, where she files everything.&lt;/p&gt;[[Wipe your mouth, get back to work.-&gt;Location_Renner&#39;s_Depot]]
[IMAGE MISSING] sex/renner_loop.jpg&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;She locks the office door. He&#39;s already reaching for her — the cold boss gone, just a wrecked man who&#39;s spent all day waiting for the help to come and take him apart.&lt;/p&gt;

